---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Acceptable Use Policy — Finicium Capital"
  description="Read the Acceptable Use Policy for Finicium Capital LTD. This policy outlines the acceptable and prohibited uses of our website and services."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header-bg"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-header-title animate-on-scroll">Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--compact">
    <div class="container legal-content">
      <p class="last-updated">Last updated: 22 February 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>This Acceptable Use Policy ("Policy") sets out the rules governing the use of the Finicium Capital LTD ("we," "our," or "us") website and any related services. By accessing our website, you agree to comply with this Policy. If you do not agree with these terms, you must not use our website.</p>
      <p>This Policy should be read in conjunction with our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. Permitted Use</h2>
      <p>You may use our website for lawful purposes only. Permitted uses include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Viewing and accessing publicly available content on the website.</li>
        <li>Submitting enquiries through our contact form for legitimate business purposes.</li>
        <li>Sharing links to our website content, provided proper attribution is given.</li>
        <li>Accessing information about our company, technology, and services.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Prohibited Activities</h2>
      <p>You must not use our website to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Engage in any activity that is unlawful, fraudulent, or harmful.</li>
        <li>Transmit or distribute any material that is defamatory, obscene, threatening, abusive, or otherwise objectionable.</li>
        <li>Send unsolicited or unauthorised advertising, promotional materials, or spam.</li>
        <li>Knowingly introduce viruses, trojans, worms, logic bombs, or other material that is malicious or technologically harmful.</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to our website, the server on which it is hosted, or any server, computer, or database connected to our website.</li>
        <li>Attack our website via a denial-of-service attack or a distributed denial-of-service attack.</li>
        <li>Interfere with or disrupt the integrity or performance of our website or the experience of other users.</li>
        <li>Scrape, harvest, or extract data from our website using automated tools without our written permission.</li>
        <li>Impersonate any person or entity, or falsely state or misrepresent your affiliation with any person or entity.</li>
        <li>Use the website in any manner that could damage, disable, overburden, or impair our infrastructure.</li>
        <li>Reproduce, duplicate, copy, sell, resell, or exploit any portion of the website without express written permission.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>All intellectual property rights in the website and its content belong to Finicium Capital LTD or our licensors. You must not use any content from our website in any way that infringes our intellectual property rights or those of any third party. Any unauthorised use may give rise to a claim for damages and could constitute a criminal offence.</p>

      <h2>5. Reporting Violations</h2>
      <p>If you become aware of any activity that violates this Policy, we encourage you to report it to us immediately at <a href="mailto:info@finiciumcapital.com">info@finiciumcapital.com</a>. We will investigate all reports and take appropriate action.</p>

      <h2>6. Enforcement</h2>
      <p>We reserve the right to take any action we deem appropriate if you breach this Policy, including but not limited to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Issuing a formal warning.</li>
        <li>Temporarily or permanently restricting access to our website.</li>
        <li>Commencing legal proceedings against you for reimbursement of all costs resulting from the breach, including reasonable legal fees.</li>
        <li>Reporting the matter to law enforcement authorities where we reasonably believe a criminal offence has been committed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may revise this Acceptable Use Policy at any time by updating this page. You are expected to check this page periodically to take notice of any changes, as they are legally binding on you. Some of the provisions contained in this Policy may also be superseded by provisions or notices published elsewhere on our website.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions about this Acceptable Use Policy, please contact us:</p>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@finiciumcapital.com">info@finiciumcapital.com</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    position: relative;
    padding: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--space-20)) 0 var(--space-8);
    text-align: center;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .page-header-bg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: var(--gradient-hero);
  }
  .page-header-bg::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 200px;
    background: linear-gradient(to top, var(--color-bg-primary), transparent);
  }
  .page-header .container {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .page-header-title {
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 4vw, var(--text-5xl));
  }
</style>
